1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:05,070
This is Account Access. In this walkthrough, we'll install it and use it with

2
00:00:05,070 --> 00:00:10,350
Codex and Claude Code. Everything you see uses fictional demo accounts, with no personal

3
00:00:10,350 --> 00:00:11,489
passwords required.

4
00:00:13,033 --> 00:00:17,829
You'll need Git, the u v package manager, and your preferred AI agent already

5
00:00:17,829 --> 00:00:22,127
installed and signed in. The written guide links to u v installation.

6
00:00:22,127 --> 00:00:26,238
This video uses a Mac; Linux has extra browser setup instructions.

7
00:00:27,783 --> 00:00:30,310
First, clone the public GitHub repository.

8
00:00:30,310 --> 00:00:32,896
Then change into the account access folder.

9
00:00:32,896 --> 00:00:36,806
All installation commands in the next steps run from this folder.

10
00:00:38,367 --> 00:00:42,671
Run these three commands. The first prepares Python and the dependencies.

11
00:00:42,671 --> 00:00:46,150
The second installs the browser used by website connectors.

12
00:00:46,150 --> 00:00:48,568
The third builds the installable package.

13
00:00:48,568 --> 00:00:50,750
The first run can take a few minutes.

14
00:00:52,283 --> 00:00:54,771
Install the package as a command line tool.

15
00:00:54,771 --> 00:00:59,400
If your terminal cannot find account access afterward, run u v tool update shell

16
00:00:59,400 --> 00:01:03,972
and open a new terminal. The guide also covers a missing Python three launcher.

17
00:01:05,533 --> 00:01:07,409
Start the demo with this command.

18
00:01:07,409 --> 00:01:12,468
It prepares three fictional accounts and installs the Account Access skill for both Codex

19
00:01:12,468 --> 00:01:14,798
and Claude Code. Keep this terminal open.

20
00:01:14,798 --> 00:01:19,061
The demo handles its test credentials and authenticator code automatically.

21
00:01:20,617 --> 00:01:23,408
In a second terminal, run the connection check.

22
00:01:23,408 --> 00:01:26,200
Look for status O K and service reachable true.

23
00:01:26,200 --> 00:01:30,238
That confirms the installed client can reach the local demo service.

24
00:01:31,783 --> 00:01:34,764
Open a fresh Codex chat and paste this prompt.

25
00:01:34,764 --> 00:01:40,208
Codex discovers the accounts, creates a task, waits for it, and reports the results.

26
00:01:40,208 --> 00:01:44,096
Our actual Codex command line run completed all three reads.

27
00:01:44,096 --> 00:01:46,753
You don't type the demo password or code.

28
00:01:48,283 --> 00:01:52,754
In Claude Code, start a fresh session and use slash account access with the

29
00:01:52,754 --> 00:01:57,642
same request. The service is shared, while each agent has its own client identity.

30
00:01:57,642 --> 00:02:01,457
This actual Claude Code run also completed all three demo reads.

31
00:02:03,033 --> 00:02:06,395
For a real account, a reviewed connector must exist first.

32
00:02:06,395 --> 00:02:11,438
Then owner setup lets you enter credentials locally, connect or repair the account, and

33
00:02:11,438 --> 00:02:13,931
choose the operations an agent may perform.

34
00:02:13,931 --> 00:02:17,815
The demo has already prepared its accounts and permissions for you.

35
00:02:19,367 --> 00:02:22,413
Today, passwords are entered once in local setup.

36
00:02:22,413 --> 00:02:26,827
An enrolled authenticator secret lets the service generate login codes.

37
00:02:26,827 --> 00:02:31,366
Gmail and Twilio adapters exist, but live code delivery is not validated.

38
00:02:31,366 --> 00:02:35,967
Personal phone inbox access and password manager import are not built yet.

39
00:02:37,533 --> 00:02:40,643
If the skill is missing, open a fresh agent session.

40
00:02:40,643 --> 00:02:43,154
If the service is unavailable, restart it.

41
00:02:43,154 --> 00:02:48,117
Needs user means complete the specified step in owner setup, then continue the same

42
00:02:48,117 --> 00:02:51,346
task. Denied means review the permissions you granted.

43
00:02:52,867 --> 00:02:55,465
You're ready to try the three account demo.

44
00:02:55,465 --> 00:03:00,783
The repository has every command, the captioned video, and the real account setup guide.

45
00:03:00,783 --> 00:03:07,006
This is a release candidate; arbitrary websites, banks, and insurance accounts still require connectors

46
00:03:07,006 --> 00:03:07,732
and testing.
